>> title: Shio Ramen
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: chicken, japanese, ramen, noodles, salt
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: shio ramen, 塩ラーメン, salt ramen, clear ramen, Hakodate ramen, a bowl of shio, shio-ramen
>> pairs-with: chintan-broth, dashi, shio-tare, ramen-noodles, chashu, ajitama
>> servings: 1
>> time: 10 min

>> step: The palest bowl and the least forgiving — a thin broth, a salt seasoning, and no colour to cover anything up.
The palest bowl and the least forgiving — a thin broth, a salt seasoning, and no colour to cover anything up.

>> step: spoon the tare and chicken fat into a scalded bowl
Ladle @shio tare{1 1/2%Tbs}(22 mL) and @chicken fat{2%tsp}(10 mL; lifted off the chilled chintan) into a scalded #ramen bowl{}.

>> step: pour the broth, cut with dashi, boiling
Pour @chintan broth{1%cup}(240 mL; at a full boil) and @dashi{1/2%cup}(120 mL; at a full boil) into @&(~1)tare and fat{} and stir once.

>> step: boil 60 sec, drain hard
Boil @ramen noodles{5%oz}(140 g; 1.5 mm straight) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L; hard-boiling, unsalted) ~boil{60%sec}, then lift and shake the basket dry.

>> step: lay the noodles in, straightened with chopsticks
Lift @&(~1)drained noodles{} into @&(~2)seasoned broth{} and straighten them with chopsticks.

>> step: lay the toppings, yuzu at the end
Lay @chāshū{2%slices}(warmed), @ajitama{1/2}(halved lengthways), @kamaboko{2%slices}(steamed fish cake), @scallion{1%stalk}(thinly sliced) and @yuzu zest{1%pinch}(pared, no pith) over @&(~1)bowl{}.
